      "id": "1002",
      "title": "Kubernetes for the rest of us",
      "description": "You do not need a platform team of twenty to run Kubernetes well. This talk walks through a small team's setup: one cluster per environment, a boring ingress, managed databases, and the handful of operational habits that keep it that way.\r\n\r\nExpect opinions, a few war stories and a checklist you can take home.",
      "startsAt": "2030-05-15T10:00:00",
